10.1214/aop/1015345757: HTTP 200 | 'Bootstrapping the Student t-Statistic' | 'The Annals of Probability' vol 29 issue 4 page 1435-1450 | published [[2001, 10, 1]]
   abstract:  Let $X_1\ldots,X_n, n \geq 1$, be independent, identically distributed random variables and consider the Student $t$-statistic $T_n$ based upon these random variables. Giné, Götze and Mason (1997) proved that $T_n$ converges in distribution to a standard normal random variable if and only if $X$ is in the domain of attraction of a normal random variable and$EX = 0$. We shall show that roughly the same holds true for the bootstrapped Student $t$- statistic $T_n^*$. In the process we shall disclose all the possible subsequential limiting laws of $T_^*n$. The proofs introduce a number of amusing
